<title>USA: NYPA Indian Pt 3 nuke seen at full power Monday.</title>
<headline>NYPA Indian Pt 3 nuke seen at full power Monday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York Power Authority's 965 megawatt Indian Point nuclear power unit 3 was expected to reach full power Monday after reducing output Sunday for a valve repair, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect it to return to full power later today,&quot; spokesman Joseph Leary said Monday.</p>
<p>The unit was holding electricity production at about 60 percent of capacity during the repairs, which Leary said involved a minor valve leak.</p>
<p>The Indian Point unit is located at Buchanan, N.Y.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
